Enhance Quantum Exposure Graph™ into an Enterprise Cryptographic Dependency & Migration Intelligence Platform

In http://localhost:3000/dashboard/quantum-readiness/exposure-graph, redesign and significantly enhance the Quantum Exposure Graph™ into a comprehensive Enterprise Cryptographic Dependency Graph, Migration Impact Analysis Engine, and Trust Relationship Visualization.

The goal is to provide customers with complete visibility into how their assets, cryptographic systems, certificates, trust relationships, APIs, cloud services, third-party vendors, and business applications are interconnected, enabling them to safely plan and execute quantum migration with minimal operational risk.

This should become one of the flagship capabilities of QGuard Helix and differentiate it from traditional vulnerability management and asset inventory platforms.

Primary Objectives

The Quantum Exposure Graph™ should help customers answer critical business and technical questions, including:

Which assets are connected to each other?
Which systems depend on one another?
Which assets communicate with external or third-party services?
Which third-party vendors or SaaS platforms still use quantum-vulnerable cryptography?
Which assets are most critical to business operations?
Which systems should be migrated first?
Which systems must be migrated together?
What services, applications, or trust relationships may break if an asset is upgraded?
What is the blast radius if a migration fails?
How can migrations be sequenced to minimize downtime and operational risk?

The platform should transform complex cryptographic relationships into intuitive, interactive visualizations that enable informed migration planning.

